The query is specified by the following JSON-like structure, assuming a standard grammar for the query language. The target is "Film", and the WHERE clause uses existential quantifiers to find films that have at least one director and at least one actor, with the additional condition that there exists at least one director and one actor (possibly the same person) who share the same surname.

```json
{
  "target": "Film",
  "where": {
    "and": [
      {
        "exists": {
          "rel": "director",
          "to": "x"
        }
      },
      {
        "exists": {
          "rel": "actor",
          "to": "y"
        }
      },
      {
        "eq": [
          {
            "attr": {
              "of": "x",
              "attr": "surname"
            }
          },
          {
            "attr": {
              "of": "y",
              "attr": "surname"
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

This query ensures that the film has a director (specified by the "rel": "director" relation) and an actor (specified by the "rel": "actor" relation), and that the surname of the director (accessed via "attr": "surname" of "x") matches the surname of the actor (accessed via "attr": "surname" of "y"). The variables "x" and "y" are bound by the existential quantifiers to specific persons for the film.

